WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.197
The results consistently favor the proposed recipe.

00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:05.382
On the mixed three-task benchmark,

00:00:05.462 --> 00:00:11.808
balancing the data through augmentation beats both
the raw unbalanced mixture and naive re-sampling,

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.700
which actually collapses on the scarce tasks.

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:19.391
Knowledge distillation then improves the compact
student on segmentation,

00:00:19.471 --> 00:00:24.275
pose estimation, and deraining, in both single-task
and multi-task training.

00:00:24.355 --> 00:00:27.809
On the Pascal five-i foreground segmentation benchmark,

00:00:27.889 --> 00:00:34.942
the distilled and fine-tuned three-hundred-million
model clearly surpasses the same model trained from scratch.

00:00:35.022 --> 00:00:40.661
And scaling data on segmentation from one to ten
percent lowers validation loss by nearly

00:00:40.741 --> 00:00:44.003
two tenths and perplexity by over twenty-two points,

00:00:44.083 --> 00:00:47.730
an effect augmentation reproduces with no new data at all.
